            answer: "A",
            solution: `<p>The recursion starts from level 1 and goes to level 3.</p>
<p>At each level, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>pw_global</mi></math> is updated:<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>level</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>level</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>level</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />&nbsp;So the total becomes 6.</p>
<p>At level 3, longjmp is called with temp set to 30.</p>
<p>This immediately jumps back to the setjmp call in main, skipping all remaining recursive calls and print statements.</p>
<p>So no "Backtracking" lines are printed.</p>
<p>The value returned by setjmp becomes 30, so control goes to the else block.</p>
<p>Final output is: &nbsp;30 6</p>`
