            solution: `<p>The switch has no breaks between cases, so fall-through happens.</p>
<p>Start with i = 0:</p>
<p>&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>case</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>fall</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>through</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>case</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>fall</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>through</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>case</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>fall</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>through</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>default</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p>
<p>Print: 16<br />Then loop increment <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> i becomes 17</p>
<p>Next iteration i = 17:</p>
<p>No case matches <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> directly default<br />&nbsp;i = 17 + 4 = 21</p>
<p>Print: 21<br />Then loop increment <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>i becomes 22<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>loop ends</p>
<p>Final output:&nbsp;16 21</p>`
