            neg: 0.33,
            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p>The set&nbsp; T represents various traversals over a binary tree. The set S represents the order of visiting nodes during a traversal.</p>
<p>T</p>
<p>I: Inorder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; II: Preorder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; III: Postorder</p>
<p>S</p>
<p>L: left subtree, node, right subtree&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; M: node, left subtree, right subtree&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; N: left subtree, right subtree, node</p>
<p>Which one of the following is the correct match from T to S?</p>`,
