            solution: `<p>strcmp returns: negative if s1&lt; s2, 0 if equal, positive if s1&gt;s2.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>strcmp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PWGATE</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mo>"</mo></math> is a proper prefix; the terminating \\0 in s1 compares less than 'G' in s2. The result is negative.&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is 1.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>strcmp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mn>2027</mn><mo>"</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mn>2025</mn><mo>"</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>:</mo></math> equal up to index 4, at index 5 we compare '7' vs '5'. '7' &gt; '5', so the result is positive.&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is 1.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>strcmp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>PW</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>equal</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>strings</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>returns</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>Sum</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
