            answer: 11,
            solution: `<p>A 2D array int&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>arr</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math> is stored in row-major order as a single contiguous block of<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math> ints.</p>
<p>Linear index of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>arr</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>*</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi></math> (since the row length is 4).</p>
<p>arr[0][0] &rarr; linear index 0.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>arr</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>linear</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>index</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>*</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Both p and q are int *, pointing into the same underlying array, so the pointer subtraction&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi></math> is well-defined.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
