            type: "MSQ",
            text: `<p>Consider a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) data structure with union by rank and path compression, operating on elements <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>The following union operations are performed (Union always attaches the lower-rank tree under the higher-rank):</p>
<p>Union(1,2), Union(3,4), Union(5,6), Union(7,8)</p>
<p>Union(1,3), Union(5,7)</p>
<p>Union(1,5)</p>
<p>Which of the following statements is/are TRUE after all union operations?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p>Find(6) returns the same representative as Find(2)</p>`,
                `<p>The final tree has height at most 3</p>`,
                `<p>The rank of the root is exactly 3</p>`,
                `<p>Find(4) and Find(7) return the same representative</p>`,
            ],
            answer: ["A", "B", "C", "D"],
            solution: `<p>Round 1:</p>
<p>Union(1,2): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, tree: 1<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&larr;</mo></math>2<br />Union(3,4): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, tree: 3<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&larr;</mo></math>4<br />Union(5,6): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, tree: 5<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&larr;</mo></math>6<br />Union(7,8): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, tree: 7<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&larr;</mo></math>8</p>
<p>Round 2:</p>
<p>Union(1,3): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>attach 3 under 1, rank[1] becomes 2. Tree: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>1</mn><mo>&larr;</mo><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&larr;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Union(5,7): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>attach 7 under 5, rank[5] becomes 2. Tree: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>5</mn><mo>&larr;</mo><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&larr;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p>Round 3:</p>
<p>Union(1,5): <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>attach 5 under 1, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math> becomes 3.</p>
<ol>
<li>Find(6) the same representative as Find(2)? Both are under root 1. TRUE</li>
<li>Height at most 3? Path <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>has 4 nodes = height 3 edges. With height = number of edges, height = 3. TRUE</li>
<li>Rank of root is exactly 3? <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>rank</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>TRUE</li>
<li>Find(4) and Find(7) return the same representative? Both reach root 1. TRUE</li>
</ol>`
