            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p>The Next Greater Element (NGE) of a number x in an array is the first element to the right of x that is greater than x. If no such element exists, its NGE is &minus;1.</p>
<p>A stack-based algorithm computes NGE by processing the array from left to right:</p>
<ul>
<li>While the current element is greater than the stack top, the stack top is popped.</li>
<li>Elements remaining in the stack after the traversal are not physically popped; they are simply assigned NGE = &minus;1.</li>
</ul>
<p>Consider the array: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>]</mo></math></p>
<p>How many total pop operations during traversal are performed?</p>`,
