            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p style="text-align: justify;">The edit distance (the minimum number of insert, delete, or replace operations) between the strings "SUNDAY" and "SATURDAY" is 3.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Now consider a restricted version in which only insert and delete operations are allowed (no replaces). What is the edit distance between "SUNDAY" and "SATURDAY" under this restriction?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p>3</p>`,
                `<p>4</p>`,
                `<p>5</p>`,
                `<p>6</p>`,
            ],
            answer: "B",
            solution: `<p>When replacement is not allowed, a replacement of one character must be done as a delete + insert = 2 operations.</p>
<p><strong>Standard edit distance = 3</strong> using operations:</p>
<ul>
<li>S_NDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>SATURDAY requires: insert A, insert T, insert R (or equivalently: the optimal alignment uses 1 replace and 2 inserts, or 3 inserts+some deletes).</li>
</ul>
<p>Edit distance between SUNDAY(6) and SATURDAY(8):</p>
<p>The LCS of SUNDAY and SATURDAY =?</p>
<p>SUNDAY: S, U, N, D, A, Y SATURDAY: S, A, T, U, R, D, A, Y</p>
<p>Common subsequence: S, U, D, A, Y<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>length 5</p>
<ul>
<li>S(pos1 in both)</li>
<li>U(pos2 in SUNDAY, pos4 in SATURDAY)</li>
<li>D(pos4 in SUNDAY, pos6 in SATURDAY)</li>
<li>A(pos5 in SUNDAY, pos7 in SATURDAY)</li>
<li>Y(pos6 in SUNDAY, pos8 in SATURDAY)</li>
</ul>
<p>LCS length = <strong>5</strong> (SUDAY... actually S, U, D, A, Y = 5 chars).</p>
<p><strong>Edit distance with only insert/delete:</strong> = <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>- 2&times;LCS(X,Y) <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>5</mn></math> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>
<p>SUDAY as a common subsequence:<br />● S: SUNDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=S, SATURDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=S<br />● U: SUNDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=U, SATURDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=U (after S at pos1)<br />● D: SUNDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=D, SATURDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=D (after U at pos4)<br />● A: SUNDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=A, SATURDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=A (after D at pos6)<br />● Y: SUNDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=Y, SATURDAY<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=Y<br />LCS = SUNDAY, length 5</p>
<p>Edit distance (insert+delete only) <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>
<p>So the answer is <strong>B 4</strong>.&nbsp;</p>`
