            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p>Consider the recurrence:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mi>logn</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mtext>&emsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Which of the following is the correct asymptotic solution?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
            ],
            answer: "C",
            solution: `<p>Since the Master Theorem doesn't apply cleanly, use the <strong>recursion tree method</strong>.</p>
<p>At each level k of the recursion tree:</p>
<ul>
<li>Number of subproblems = <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></math></li>
<li>Each subproblem has size<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></math></li>
<li>Cost per subproblem<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>logn</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math></li>
<li>Total cost at level k <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&times;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>^</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>logn</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>logn</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math></li>
</ul>
<p>There are<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>levels</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Total cost = sum over k from 0 to log n - 1 of n/(log n - k)</p>
<p>Let j = log n - k, so as k goes 0<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>log n - 1, j goes log n<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>1:</p>
<p>Total <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&times;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Sigma;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi>to</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>log</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p>where H(m) is the m-th harmonic number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&asymp;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p><strong>Total cost </strong><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p><strong>Correct answer: C</strong></p>`
