            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>Consider QuickSort using the Lomuto partition scheme. The partition function for array segment A[low..high] works as follows:<br />Partition(A, low, high):<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; pivot = A[high]&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; // last element as pivot<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>low</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />for j = low to high-1:<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>if</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>pivot</mi><mo>:</mo></math><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math><br />swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>high</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math><br />return i+1<br />Consider the array: A = [7, 2, 1, 6, 8, 5, 3, 4] (low=0, high=7, 0-indexed)<br />After one call to Partition(A, 0, 7):<br />1. What is the final position (0-indexed) of the pivot element?<br />2. How many swaps (including the final pivot swap) are performed?<br />Report your answer as: (final pivot position) &times; 10 + (number of swaps)</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 34,
            solution: `<p>Array: [7, 2, 1, 6, 8, 5, 3, 4], low=0, high=7</p>
<p>pivot = A[7] = 4 i = -1</p>
<p>Trace j from 0 to 6:</p>
<p>j=0, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=7: 7<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i stay -1.</p>
<p>j=1, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=2: 2 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i=0. swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math>. Array: [2, 7, 1, 6, 8, 5, 3, 4] Swap count: 1</p>
<p>j=2, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=1: 1 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i=1. swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math>. Array: [2, 1, 7, 6, 8, 5, 3, 4] Swap count: 2</p>
<p>j=3, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=6: 6 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i stay 1.</p>
<p>j=4, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=8: 8 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i stay 1.</p>
<p>j=5, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=5: 5 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>I stay</p>
<p>j=6, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo></math>=3: 3 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&le;</mo></math>4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rArr;</mo></math>i=2. swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Array: [2, 1, 3, 6, 8, 5, 7, 4] Swap count: 3</p>
<p>Loop ends. Final swap: swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>high</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo></math> = swap<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Array: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>]</mo></math></p>
<p>Swap count: 4</p>
<p><strong>Pivot 4 is now at index 3.</strong></p>
<p>Verify: Elements left of index <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi>all</mi><mo>&le;</mo><mn>4</mn></math> Elements right of index <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>3</mn><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi>all</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>
<p><strong>Final pivot position = 3</strong> <strong>Number of swaps = 4</strong></p>
<p><strong>Correct answer: 3 &times; 10 + 4 = 34</strong></p>`
