            type: "MSQ",
            text: `<p>In Randomised QuickSort, the pivot is chosen uniformly at random from the current subarray at each step. Let C(n) be the expected number of comparisons to sort an array of n distinct elements.</p>
<p>Which of the following recurrence relations correctly describes C(n)?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></munderover><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>nlogn</mi></math></p>`,
                `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></math></p>`,
            ],
            answer: ["A", "B"],
            solution: `<p>When pivot is the k-th smallest element (probability 1/n for each k from 1 to n):</p>
<ul>
<li>We make n&minus;1 comparisons in the partition step</li>
<li>Left subarray has k&minus;1 elements, right has n&minus;k elements</li>
</ul>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></munderover><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></math></p>
<p>Since the sum</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mrow><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></munderover><mo>[</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></math></p>
<p>counts each C(0),C(1),...,C(n-1) exactly twice:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>For large n,<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&asymp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></math>, so this is approximately:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&asymp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&sum;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>which is option B.</p>
<p>Solving option A also gives the same result. Hence, A is also correct.</p>`
