            text: `<p>A milkman has two types of milk solutions. Solution A has milk and water in a ratio of 7:3. Solution B has milk and water in a ratio of 3:7. In what ratio must A and B be mixed so that the resulting mixture has equal amounts of milk and water?</p>`,
