            answer: "C",
            solution: `<p>The policymaker assumes correlation implies causation. Option C offers an alternative explanation for the observed correlation by introducing a variable (municipal funding) that explains both outcomes independently, so libraries don't cause literacy; they just co-occur. A doesn't disprove the general trend. B talks about feasibility, not logic. D is irrelevant to the causal claim.</p>`
