            text: `<p>Consider the following schedule with transactions T1 and T2 using Two-Phase Locking:</p>
<p>T1: Lock-X(A), Read(A), Write(A), Lock-X(B), Read(B), Write(B), Unlock(A), Unlock(B)</p>
<p>T2: Lock-X(A), Read(A), Write(A), Unlock(A)</p>
<p>T1 and T2 run concurrently. T2 requests Lock-X(A) after T1 has already acquired Lock-X(A) but before T1 releases it.</p>
<p>How many times is T2 forced to WAIT before it can complete execution?</p>`,
            image: "",
