            text: `<p>The selective repeat protocol has a maximum window size of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mn>2</mn><mpadded voffset="-1px"><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mpadded></msup></math>, where n is the number of bits in the sequence number field. Why can't the window size be <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msup></math>?</p>`,
