            marks: 2,
            neg: 0,
            type: "MSQ",
            text: `<p>Consider the producer-consumer problem solved using semaphores with: mutex (init=1), empty (init=N), full (init=0). Which of the following are correct?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p>The producer does wait(empty) before wait(mutex); reversing this order can cause deadlock.</p>`,
                `<p>Consumer does wait(full) before wait(mutex).</p>`,
                `<p>If the producer does wait(mutex) before wait(empty), deadlock can occur when the buffer is full.</p>`,
                `<p>The mutex semaphore ensures only one producer or consumer accesses the buffer at a time.</p>`,
            ],
            answer: ["A", "B", "C", "D"],
            solution: `<p>Standard solution:</p>
<p>Producer: wait(empty)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>wait(mutex)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>add item<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>signal(mutex)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>signal(full).<br />Consumer: wait(full)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>wait(mutex)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>remove item<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>signal(mutex)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>signal(empty).</p>
<p>A: True. If the producer does wait(mutex) first, then wait(empty): when the buffer is full (empty=0), the producer holds the mutex and waits on empty. Consumers need a mutex to consume blocked. Deadlock.</p>
<p>B: True. The consumer waits on full first (ensures something to consume), then mutex. Correct order.</p>
<p>C: True. Directly follows from A's explanation.</p>
<p>D: True. A mutex is a binary semaphore protecting the buffer from mutual exclusion between all producers/consumers.</p>`
