            text: `<p>Which of the following are necessary conditions for deadlock (Coffman's conditions)?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p>Mutual exclusion</p>`,
                `<p>Hold and wait</p>`,
                `<p>Preemption allowed</p>`,
                `<p>Circular wait</p>`,
            ],
            answer: ["A", "B", "D"],
            solution: `<p>Coffman's four necessary conditions for deadlock:</p>
<ol>
<li>Mutual exclusion: at least one resource is held in a non-shareable mode.</li>
<li>Hold and wait: a process holds one resource and waits for more.</li>
<li>No preemption resources can be forcibly taken.</li>
<li>Circular wait is a circular chain of processes waiting for each other.</li>
</ol>
<p>A: TRUE.</p>
<p>B: TRUE.</p>
<p>C: "Preemption allowed" is the OPPOSITE of the condition; the condition is NO preemption. FALSE.</p>
<p>D: TRUE.</p>`
