            image: "",
            options: [
                `<p>The first request serviced is cylinder 43</p>`,
                `<p>Total head movement is 208</p>`,
                `<p>SSTF can cause starvation of requests far from the current head position</p>`,
                `<p>SSTF always provides better throughput than FCFS</p>`,
            ],
            answer: ["A", "B", "C"],
            solution: `<p>SSTF always services the closest pending request to the current head.</p>
<p>From 50: distances 82(32), 170(120), 43(7), 140(90), 24(26), 16(34), 190(140). Closest = 43.</p>
<p>A: First request = 43. TRUE.</p>
<p>B. Compute full sequence: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>50</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>43</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>82</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>170</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>190</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Movement:&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>208</mn><mo>.</mo></math> B says 208. TRUE.</p>
<p>C: Requests far from the current cluster of requests can be indefinitely postponed as new, closer requests keep arriving. TRUE.</p>
<p>D: FALSE. SSTF generally gives better throughput than FCFS, but not ALWAYS in specific access patterns; FCFS can match or exceed SSTF throughput. "Always" makes D false.</p>`
