            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>Evaluate the improper integral as ln(A). What is the value of A:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><msub><mo>&int;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&infin;</mo></msup><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>dx</mi></math></p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 2,
            solution: `<p>Partial fractions:&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><msub><mo>&int;</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&infin;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>dx</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>lnx</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&infin;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&infin;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>&infin;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>At x=1: ln(1/2) = &minus;ln2.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>Integral</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
