            text: `<p>Using Sethi-Ullman labelling, find the minimum number of registers needed to evaluate:<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>*</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>*</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">h</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 4,
            solution: `<p>Using the Sethi-Ullman labelling algorithm:</p>
<ul>
<li>Each leaf (a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h) has label 1.</li>
<li>(a+b) has two equal children (1,1), so its label is 2.</li>
<li>(c+d) also has label 2.</li>
<li>The multiplication node ((a+b)*(c+d)) has two equal children (2,2), so its label is 3.</li>
<li>Similarly, ((e+f)*(g+h)) also has label 3.</li>
<li>Finally, the root&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>*</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>*</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">h</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math> has two equal children (3,3), so its label is 4.</li>
</ul>
<p>Therefore, the minimum number of registers required is 4.</p>`
