            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>Consider a stack-based runtime environment (no registers, pure stack machine) executing recursive function calls. Function f has an activation record of size 40 bytes (including locals, saved registers, return address). If f calls itself recursively with a maximum recursion depth of 100, and the initial stack pointer is at address 10000 growing DOWNWARD, what is the stack pointer value at the point of DEEPEST recursion (just after the 100th call's AR is fully pushed, before any local variable modifications)?</p>`,
