            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>Consider the language L over <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&#931;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>}</mo><mo>:</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>}</mo><mo>*</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>|</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi></math> ends with <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>"</mo><mi>aba</mi><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">}</mi></math></p>
<p>Using the Myhill-Nerode theorem, what is the minimum number of states in any DFA accepting L?</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 4,
            solution: `<p>The Myhill-Nerode equivalence classes are defined by the right-invariant equivalence: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&equiv;</mo><mi>_Ly</mi></math> iff for all <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mo>&isin;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Sigma;</mi><mo>*</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>xz</mi><mo>&isin;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>&harr;</mo><mi>yz</mi><mo>&isin;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math>.</p>
<p>Each equivalence class corresponds to one state in the minimal DFA. The classes are determined by the longest suffix of x that is a prefix of "aba":</p>
<p>&nbsp;Class q0: no suffix of x is a prefix of "aba". (<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&epsilon;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>bb</mi></math>)<br />&nbsp;Class q1: longest matching prefix = "a". (e.g., x ends with a but not ab)<br />&nbsp;Class q2: longest matching prefix = "ab". (e.g., x ends with ab)<br />&nbsp;Class q3: x ends with "aba" <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&isin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math>. (accept state)</p>
<p>These 4 classes are distinguishable:<br />&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>vs</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo></math> string <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>"</mo><mi>ba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>ba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&notin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>ba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&notin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math>. Try <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>"</mo><mi>aba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>aba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&isin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>aba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>aaba</mi><mo>"</mo></math> ends with aba&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&isin;</mo></math>L. Both go to L. Try: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>"</mo></math>. <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>"</mo><mi>bba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&notin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math> but adding <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&rarr;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>ba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&notin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math>. Try <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>ba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>bba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&notin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>"</mo><mi>aba</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&isin;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></math>. Distinguished.</p>
<p>All 4 classes are distinct <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math> minimum DFA has 4 states.</p>`
