            text: `<p>The Post Correspondence Problem (PCP) is known to be undecidable in general. A common but flawed intuition suggests that restricting the alphabet size should always make the problem "easier" in a smooth, monotonic way as&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Sigma;</mi><mo>|</mo></math> shrinks. Test this intuition against the known decidability boundary and identify which assertion about PCP is CORRECT.</p>`,
