            solution: `<p>Introduce&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The rule&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi>aXb</mi></math> becomes <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></msub></math>, which binarises into <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi>XT</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The rule&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi>aX</mi></math> becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The rule&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></math> is already length 1 (a valid CNF terminal rule) and needs no further change. Final rule set: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi>XT</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></msub></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&rarr;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></math> 6 rules total.</p>`
