            text: `<p>Inherent ambiguity is a property of the language itself (every possible CFG for it is ambiguous), not merely a property of one poorly designed grammar, so a language is NOT disqualified just because someone can also find an unambiguous-looking grammar attempt for it that turns out, on closer inspection, to still be ambiguous or simply wrong. With that distinction firmly in mind, and considering that palindromes have a well-known unambiguous grammar while aⁿbⁿ trivially does too, identify which of the following languages is inherently ambiguous, i.e., admits absolutely no unambiguous CFG.</p>`,
