            answer: ["D"],
            solution: `<p>Under the CFL pumping lemma, the constraint |vwx| &le; p means vwx can span at most two of the three symbol blocks {a,b,c}. Option (A) violates&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>|</mo><mi>vx</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&ge;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> outright. Options (B) and (C) either violate&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>|</mo><mi>vwx</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&le;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">p</mi></math> in general or, when valid, change the count of at most two of the three symbol types upon pumping, which necessarily breaks the required triple equality <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>ⁿ</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>ⁿ</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mo>ⁿ</mo><mo>.</mo></math> None of the adversary's decompositions escapes a contradiction.</p>`
