            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p>DPDAs accepting by empty stack are constrained by the prefix property: no proper prefix of a string in the language can itself belong to the language, since reaching an empty stack partway through processing would force early (incorrect) acceptance. This creates a subtle gap between "accepted by empty-stack DPDA" and "accepted by final-state DPDA," since final-state acceptance carries no such restriction. Using this distinction, identify which of the following is a DCFL that IS accepted by some final-state DPDA, but for which NO DPDA can accept it via empty-stack acceptance without structural modification (i.e., identify the language that violates the prefix property).</p>`,
