            text: `<p>A write-back cache with a per-block dirty bit has a hit rate of 95% for write references. A write hit generates zero memory traffic (write stays in cache, dirty bit set). A write miss always triggers a block fetch from memory (allocate-on-write-miss), generating 32 bytes of traffic; additionally, if the block being evicted to make room is dirty, which happens for 40% of misses, an extra 32-byte write-back occurs. For 10,000 total write references from the CPU, what is the total memory traffic, in bytes, generated purely by misses?</p>`,
