            solution: `<p>For <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>ABC</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>101</mn></math> (I5), the relevant minterms are m10 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and m11 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math><br />m10 = 0 (not in the function's minterm list), <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> (in the list).<br />So output = 0 when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, output = 1 when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math>this is exactly D.<br />Hence <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi></math>.</p>`
