            answer: 3,
            solution: `<p>Minimizing F1: the quad A'D covers <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and the quad B'D' covers <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math> together they cover all of F1 exactly. Minimal <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Minimizing F2: the quad B'D' covers <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>and the quad CD covers <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math> together they cover all of F2 exactly. Minimal <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>CD</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>The term B'D' is common to BOTH functions. Distinct AND gates needed = <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>CD</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> gates total (plus 2 separate output OR gates, not asked here).</p>`
