            answer: 8,
            solution: `<p>Minterm 0 (0000) is adjacent only to minterm 4<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math> forces prime implicant <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>'</mo></math> (covers 0,4) &mdash; essential (unique coverage of minterm 0).</p>
<p>Minterms 5,7,13,15 form a genuine quad: all satisfy <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> with A,C free <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math> BD (covers 5,7,13,15) &mdash; essential (unique coverage of minterms 7 and 13, since their only adjacent present neighbors lie entirely within this quad).</p>
<p>Minterms 10,11 are adjacent only to each other <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&rarr;</mo></math> forces prime implicant AB'C (covers 10,11) &mdash; essential (unique coverage of minterms 10,11).</p>
<p>These three essential prime implicants together cover all 8 minterms exactly. Minimal SOP =<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>BD</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Literals<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
