            solution: `<p>Using the consensus theorem:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>AB</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>BC</mi></math></p>
<p>and therefore,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>Now implement this POS form using NOR gates.</p>
<p>Generate A':</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="wrs_chemistry"><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>NOR</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo></math></p>
<p>Generate the complemented sum terms:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>NOR</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>'</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>NOR</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>'</mo></math></p>
<p>Finally,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>NOR</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>'</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>'</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>'</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>BC</mi></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>AB</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi></math></p>
<p>Thus,</p>
<p>Minimum number of NOR gates = 4</p>
<p>Hence, the correct answer is (B).</p>`
