            answer: 7,
            solution: `<p>Generate A' and B': 2 inverters.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>:</mo></math> 1 AND gate.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>\\</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>:</mo></math> 1 AND gate.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>requires 2 new AND gates (A.B and A'.B', reusing existing A', B') plus 1 OR gate to combine them: 3 gates.</p>
<p>Total <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>inverters</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> = 7 gates.</p>`
