            type: "MCQ",
            text: `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo></math> Sum of minterms (0, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 13, 14)</p>
<p>This function is implemented using a single 8-to-1 multiplexer, with select lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>,</mo></math> and variable D applied externally to the appropriate data input lines (I0 through I7, corresponding to ABC = 000 through 111).</p>
<p>What signal (0, 1, D, or D') must be connected to input line I3 (selected when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)?</p>`,
