            answer: "A",
            solution: `<p>For <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>ABC</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>011</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math> the relevant minterms are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Neither m6 nor m7 appears in the given minterm list <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>&mdash; the function equals 0 for both values of D at this selected combination. Hence, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
