            type: "MSQ",
            text: `<p>A 2-way set-associative cache has a total capacity of 64 bytes and a block size of 8 bytes. It is initially empty. Byte addresses are mapped as: set index = (address / 8) mod 4. The following 12 byte addresses are accessed in order:</p>
<p>0, 64, 0, 128, 64, 0, 8, 72, 8, 136, 72, 0</p>
<p>Each access touches a single byte. Compare LRU and FIFO replacement (within a set). Which of the following is/are TRUE?</p>`,
            image: "",
