            neg: 0,
            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>The number of events N in an interval is Poisson with mean 3. Each event is independently "marked" with probability 1/3. Let M be the number of marked events. Compute <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, rounded to 3 decimal places.</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 0.089,
            solution: `<p>By Poisson thinning, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>~</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>Poisson(1) and U = N &minus; M ~ Poisson(2) are independent.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>|</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo></math> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">U</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>⁻</mo><mo>&sup2;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⁴</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>⁻</mo><mo>&sup2;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&middot;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>13534</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&times;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>66667</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&asymp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>090</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
