            answer: -0.084,
            solution: `<ul>
<li>cos <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&hellip;</mo></math></li>
<li><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mo>^</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>&hellip;</mo></math></li>
<li>The numerator is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">O</mi><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">O</mi><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></li>
<li>The denominator is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&middot;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">O</mi><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></li>
</ul>
<p>The limit is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&asymp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>083</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`
