            text: `<p>A disk has cylinders 0 to 199. The head is at cylinder 90, moving toward higher cylinders. The pending requests are 150, 45, 120, 10, 190, 60, 100. C-SCAN serves requests upward until cylinder 199, then the head returns to cylinder 0 (this return movement is counted), then serves the remaining requests upward. What is the total head movement in cylinders?</p>`,
