            neg: 0,
            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>&nbsp;Semaphores S (initial value 3) and T (initial value 0) are shared by two infinitely looping processes. wait and signal are atomic, and any interleaving is permitted.</p>
<p>P1: while(true)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi>wait</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>print</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>signal</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p>P2: while(true)<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi>wait</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>wait</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>print</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>"</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>"</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>signal</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>signal</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p>The number of distinct strings that can be the first 12 characters printed is ______.</p>`,
            image: "",
            options: [
            ],
            answer: 16,
            solution: `<ul>
<li>Let a and b be the counts of A and B printed so far.</li>
<li>The next A is allowed iff <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&le;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></math> (S tokens), and the next B is allowed iff <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&le;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&lfloor;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&rfloor;</mo></math> (T tokens).</li>
<li>Every reachable state has at least one legal move (no deadlock), so every valid prefix extends.</li>
<li>Counting paths from (0,0), with each distinct string corresponding to one path:
<ul>
<li>After 3 steps: (3,0) and (2,1).</li>
<li>After 4 steps: (3,1) has 2 paths.</li>
<li>After 6 steps: (5,1) and (4,2) each have 2 paths.</li>
<li>After 7 steps: (5,2) has 4 paths.</li>
<li>After 9 steps: (7,2) and (6,3) each have 4 paths.</li>
<li>After 10 steps: (7,3) has 8 paths.</li>
<li>After 12 steps: (9,3) and (8,4) each have 8 paths.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Total = 8 + 8 = <strong>16</strong>.</li>
</ul>`
