            type: "NAT",
            text: `<p>Strings of length 10 are formed over the alphabet <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> such that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo>&ne;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> for<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&le;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&le;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&ne;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math> How many such strings contain all three letters? ______</p>`,
